                <pb facs="0645" n="573" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg573"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10044/157.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Chargé Carter.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May 1,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 984.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The department desires you to make
                    appropriate formal expression of thanks to the British Government, on the part
                    of this Government, for the friendly action of His Majesty’s Government in
                    instructing British naval vessels in Turkish waters to afford the same
                    protection to American citizens as to British subjects in the disturbed regions
                    of Asiatic Turkey, pending the arrival of the armored cruisers which this
                    Government has dispatched to Alexandretta and Mersine.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
